[SIZE=6][B]Fastboot Studio[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]fastboot, OTA flashing, rooting, a phone page, payload dumper, super images, backups and a terminal — in one Windows app[/SIZE]

[URL='https://github.com/ifoknr/FastbootStudio/releases/latest'][B]⬇ Download[/B][/URL] · [URL='https://github.com/ifoknr/FastbootStudio']Source (GitHub)[/URL] · [URL='https://github.com/ifoknr/FastbootStudio/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md']Changelog[/URL] · [URL='https://t.me/IFOKNR1']Telegram[/URL]

[B]New in v2.5.0:[/B] a Phone page — your phone in Android, its security and its backups, with the Companion root module
[B]v2.4.0:[/B] a Root page (Magisk, KernelSU, APatch in four steps) and a boot image check that stops the usual bricks[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]What is it?[/B][/SIZE]
Fastboot Studio is a free, open-source (MIT) rewrite of [URL='https://github.com/libxzr/FastbootEnhance']Fastboot Enhance[/URL] by LibXZR. It keeps everything the original did and adds what people who flash phones reach for every day: a safe OTA flasher, image tools that replace simg2img / lpunpack / lpmake, a super image builder, and backups of partitions and files over adb.

Everything runs inside the app: no Python, no Linux tools, nothing to install. adb and fastboot (platform-tools 37.0.1) are included. English and Arabic interface, light or dark theme (or follow Windows).

[SIZE=5][B]Features[/B][/SIZE]
[B]📱 Device[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Every getvar value, every partition with its size and whether it is logical, a filter by name
[*]Flash, erase, and for logical partitions create / resize / delete
[*]Pre-flash checks: bootloader lock state, bootloader or fastbootd, pending Virtual A/B update, leftover COW partitions, current slot
[*]Reboot to system / bootloader / fastbootd / recovery, switch slot, cancel a pending update
[*][B]Boot once[/B] (fastboot boot) — refuses init_boot and vendor_boot images, which cannot start on their own, and goes through the bootloader when you are in fastbootd
[*][B]Super space[/B] — what each slot and the COW partitions take in super, and how much is free
[*][B]Boot image check[/B] — before boot, init_boot, recovery or vendor_boot is flashed, the image is unpacked (gzip, lz4, zstd, xz) and read: kernel version and KMI, security patch, and root (Magisk, KernelSU, APatch, SuSFS). An init_boot image into boot, a boot image into vendor_boot or a file that is not a boot image needs the partition name typed; a kernel built for another KMI than the phone runs (a boot-loop) or an older security patch is flagged first
[*][B]Phone in Android[/B] — the device page notices it over adb and notes its kernel and security patch for the checks above (more on the Phone page below)
[*][B]USB check[/B] — phone plugged in but not listed? It tells you why: a missing or broken driver (with the steps to fix it), Qualcomm EDL (9008), MediaTek BROM/preloader, Unisoc or Samsung download mode, or a phone still in Android (and reboots it to the bootloader)
[/LIST]

[B]📲 Phone[/B]
The phone while it runs Android, over adb — open the page and plug it in.
[LIST]
[*][B]Device[/B] — model, chip, Android and SDK, security patch, slot (A/B, dynamic), battery health and cycles, storage wear (eMMC / UFS)
[*][B]Kernel and security[/B] — kernel and KMI, bootloader locked or unlocked, SELinux, root manager, AVB state
[*][B]With the [URL='https://github.com/ifoknr/FastbootStudio-Companion']Fastboot Studio Companion[/URL] root module[/B] (Magisk, KernelSU, APatch) — the page recognises it and asks it through su: the AVB state as the [B]bootloader[/B] reported it (and a warning when a hiding module changed the property), the root manager, storage wear, and every [B]conflict between your modules[/B]: the same file from two modules, a folder one module replaces and hides from another, a property set twice. Without the module it tells you what it adds and links to it
[*][B]Backups on the phone[/B] — the Companion's backups with their kind (full, critical, boot), size and date; [B]Copy and verify[/B] brings one to the PC without root and checks every file against its SHA256SUMS
[*]Restart to bootloader, fastbootd or recovery from the page
[/LIST]

[B]⚡ Flash[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Flashes a full OTA (payload.bin or the OTA zip) in fastbootd
[*][B]Every image is extracted first, in parallel, and checked against its SHA-256 before anything is written[/B] — a broken download never reaches the phone
[*]Logical partitions the OTA needs but the phone lacks are created first; the images are checked to fit in super before writing
[*]Per-partition progress and a live fastboot log
[/LIST]

[B]🔓 Root[/B]
[LIST=1]
[*][B]Stock image[/B] — pick boot.img, init_boot.img or the whole OTA; the right image is taken out of it (init_boot for Magisk and KernelSU on Android 13+ phones that have it, boot otherwise and always for APatch), with its kernel, KMI and patch level shown
[*][B]Send it to the phone[/B] — into Download, over adb
[*][B]Patch it[/B] in Magisk, KernelSU or APatch with the steps shown, then [B]get the patched image[/B] — the newest *patched*.img is pulled and checked: root found, same kind of image, same kernel
[*][B]Flash it[/B] — the phone restarts to the bootloader and the image is written to the active slot once you type the partition name; for boot, [B]try it once first[/B] with fastboot boot
[/LIST]
The stock image is kept in Documents\Fastboot Studio\Root, to undo it.

[B]📦 Payload Dumper[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Opens payload.bin or the OTA zip directly (read in place, no unzipping)
[*]Full OTAs with every operation they use: REPLACE, ZERO, xz, bzip2, zstd…
[*]Extracts in parallel with hash checks
[/LIST]

[B]🧱 Image Tools[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Sparse ↔ raw (simg2img / img2simg), split sparse images
[*]Inspect and unpack super images (lpunpack), including split factory parts
[*]Combine Qualcomm super_1.img … super_N.img pieces using rawprogram XML
[*]Boot and init_boot images: kernel version and KMI, Android version, security patch, compression, and whether Magisk, KernelSU or APatch patched them
[/LIST]

[B]🧩 Build Super[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Builds super images byte-for-byte like AOSP lpmake (Virtual A/B, A/B, single slot)
[*]Import the layout from a phone's super, read the size from the phone
[/LIST]

[B]💾 Backup[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Partitions over adb (root, or from recovery) with SHA-256 for every image
[*]Copies files and folders from the phone (DCIM, Download…)
[*]Phone in fastboot? It reboots to recovery or boots a recovery image for you
[/LIST]

[B]⌨️ Terminal[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Run adb and fastboot commands yourself with the bundled tools, with one-click buttons for the common ones and command history
[*]Drop a file on the line to add its path; plain file names are looked up in a folder you choose
[*]Guarded like the rest of the app: flashing or erasing a critical partition, locking the bootloader or writing a block device with dd needs the name typed first, and wiping data asks first
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Safety[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Slot switch protection[/B] — warns when the other slot has not booted yet, asks in red when it is marked unbootable or out of retries, and refuses when its logical partitions are empty (as after flashing a factory super)
[*][B]Critical partitions[/B] (xbl, abl, tz, modem, persist, frp, preloader, nvdata…) can only be flashed or erased after typing the partition name
[*][B]Boot image check[/B] before flashing boot-type partitions: wrong image type, another KMI, older patch level
[*]vbmeta: offers --disable-verity --disable-verification and explains what it needs
[*]The Terminal asks the same questions before risky commands
[*]Asks before closing mid-flash
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Requirements[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Windows 10 / 11, 64-bit
[*]The phone's USB driver (e.g. Google USB Driver) — the USB check helps if it is missing
[/LIST]

[SIZE=5][B]Download & install[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST=1]
[*]Download [B]FastbootStudio-vX.Y.Z-win-x64.zip[/B] from [URL='https://github.com/ifoknr/FastbootStudio/releases/latest']GitHub Releases[/URL]
[*]Unzip it anywhere
[*]Run [B]FastbootStudio.exe[/B]
[/LIST]

